I've to add to Haakon's excellent advice and warn that the intercept is the bias of the random error and acts as the first moment of the model and thus removing it needs mathematical support. Removing it creates biased errors (even without space-time or other row based bias). I believe completeness, sufficiency, efficiency etc gets affected too ... Rudy

