Can you try
max.edge=c(0.2, 0.4)
- (or smaller)
- This is my usual recommendation for recovering matern results (which is finer than my recommendation for getting good results in general)

And make sure you only compute variogram inside the study area (the 10 by 10 area)!

PS: You may not have enough "spatial ergodicity" to compute things nicely, so you may need replicates, e.g. for precise inference on the range

Best,
Haakon

